                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8eda695c-56ff-382c-a6e3-b675d6f3353d",
                        "entry_id": "2387735c-ffa9-3282-b326-e53661f2f4cc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Tight; firm; steady; sound; in good condition or health."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dialectal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4215e010-fb02-4d22-a1e5-92d48cf566c1",
                                "sense_id": "8eda695c-56ff-382c-a6e3-b675d6f3353d",
                                "text": "Aye, the Chicopee, a fine-un, she were. Clean-built and trig-lookin’! None more fleet in ‘64 than she..."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a48f308b-b113-340f-a0b1-813d3c4fb0b9",
                        "entry_id": "2387735c-ffa9-3282-b326-e53661f2f4cc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Neat; tidy; trim; spruce; smart."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dialectal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d1947ace-c9fe-4635-b430-dfaf1f4ef875",
                                "sense_id": "a48f308b-b113-340f-a0b1-813d3c4fb0b9",
                                "text": "we possess of pig's skin and stirrups to keep them square and trig"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e284bc01-dfaa-4362-984d-5a3c77c0aa7f",
                                "sense_id": "a48f308b-b113-340f-a0b1-813d3c4fb0b9",
                                "text": "“A tight little craft,” was Austin’s invariable comment on the matron; and she looked it, always trim and trig and smooth of surface like a converted yacht cleared for action. ¶ Near her wandered her husband, orientally bland, invariably affable,[…]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b569015f-2b2b-4cf9-b7c8-878932ed151f",
                                "sense_id": "a48f308b-b113-340f-a0b1-813d3c4fb0b9",
                                "text": "The [torture] stories seemed incongruent with the men telling them – a trim, trig lot who, given a few pounds more flesh, might have stepped right out of a recruiting poster."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c9ad92d8-04f8-37d6-9286-3291c709a79b",
